Mali Utgard r4p0 kernel driver (_MALI_API_VERSION 401), the side the
user-space libMali.so (r4p0-00rel0) of FireOS 5 for ford and austin speaks.

The code is Amazon's Fire 7 (ford, MT8127) kernel's copy, as mirrored by
https://github.com/chaosmaster/android_kernel_amazon_ford
commit 5b71ce8bab684cff2534bee0175b5579f5f1b9e1
path drivers/misc/mediatek/gpu/mt8127/mali/mali, and mediatek/ from
drivers/misc/mediatek/gpu/mt8127/mediatek of the same commit: ARM's
r4p0-00rel0 with MediaTek's changes (30 files, 849 lines) and MediaTek's
platform/, mtk_common/ and Kbuild-mtk-custom-* beside it.

That copy's files carry ARM's notice for licensees of the DDK. ARM released
the same driver under GPL v2 as DX910-SW-99002-r4p0-00rel0.tgz
(http://malideveloper.arm.com/downloads/drivers/DX910/r4p0-00rel0/, now gone;
the Internet Archive's capture of 2015-03-23, sha256
0f33a31cbcd6839e4dc4588e1a0148b324de5db673a85737579af91aa89ee639, sha1 as the
capture records it). 109 of the 139 files the two have in common are the
same code. Every file here that had ARM's DDK notice has the GPL notice of
the same file in that release instead, line for line, so line numbers and
the built module's code are unchanged (2026-10-23: .text, .rodata and .data
of mali_r4p0.ko compared equal). Dropped: the three *.orig files and
linux/license/proprietary, which the GPL build never includes.
